a unique exercise in participatory  democracy the conference on the future  of Europe saw hundreds of people from  across the EU work in citizens panels to  table recommendations on how to improve  the union seven months on at a feedback  event in Brussels representatives of the  eu's three main institutions answered  questions on how they are acting on the  conferences for cruises this was not a  one-off exercise for the European Union  your proposals are not some checklist  that we need to take to close the door  on the conference on the future of  Europe once and for all  the conference proposed hundreds of  measures on areas ranging from the  environment migration and equality to  rights democracy and the eu's global  role all brought into sharp focus by the  war in Ukraine and Rising living costs  their aim is to make the EU future proof  and to deliver on citizens expectations  what we have seen is the need for social  support  in European Union  due to the crisis the need for an energy  transition for an energy Union if you  look today to the world there is more  reason to implement the conclusions of  the conference thus seven months ago  hundreds of citizens attended the event  their commitment to change and  accountability is still strong I think  we all greatly benefited from this  experience we would like to continue the  cooperation with you we would like to  look forward some kind of formal and  open Communication channel  the conference's proposals form an  important part of parliament's agenda  for 2023.  [Applause]
 

